<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Therapne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Therapne was an ancient site on the hills east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurotas">Eurotas</a>, opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a>. It held the Menelaion, a shrine where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelaus">Menelaus</a> and Helen were worshipped from the 8th century BCE. Excavations there uncovered a Mycenaean mansion of the 15th to 13th centuries BCE, one of the main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> sites of Laconia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/therapne.jpg" alt="Therapne" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George E. Koronaios · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Menelaion_(Sanctuary_of_Menelaus_and_Helen)_in_Sparta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
